  "id": "COMPOUND:980 - PROTEIN:5476",
  "verbalization": "Doxorubicin is linked to UMC-11 through a series of molecular interactions involving purinoceptors and other compounds. The evidence suggests that doxorubicin acts as a target for P2X purinoceptor 1, which is subsequently targeted by palmarumycin CP18, and this pathway leads to UMC-11. Similarly, doxorubicin is also linked to NCI-H1522, which is targeted by palmarumycin CP18, and this same compound targets UMC-11. Additionally, doxorubicin is associated with Mollicellin N, which also targets UMC-11. These findings collectively indicate that doxorubicin exerts its effects via a chain of targets that ultimately reach UMC-11, likely through the action of palmarumycin CP18. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism by which doxorubicin influences UMC-11, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
